	Generate simple tone on a channel
apifn	sm_play_tone
params	sm_play_tone_parms tonep
	The channel on which the tone is to be generated.
field	tSMChannelId channel in
	The duration of the tone, or the value zero to indicate a tone
	that will continue until explicitly aborted with
fnref	sm_play_tone_abort.
field	tSM_UT32 duration in
	An indicator of whether this function would return as soon
	as it has set up the generation of the tone (0), or wait
	until the end of the tone (non-zero).
field	tSM_INT wait_for_completion in
	The tone to generate.
field	tSM_INT tone_id in
unstruct
	This call allows an application to generate a simple output tone
	specified by
ref	tone_id
	on a given output channel
ref	channel,
	either continuously or for a given duration.
	<p>
	The parameter
ref	tone_id
	references one of the pre-loaded simple output tones, listed in
	<a href="../prospapi_outtones.html">
	Prosody speech processing: pre-loaded output tones</a>,
	or one previously defined through a call to
fnref	sm_add_output_tone.
	<p>
	If the tone is to be output continuously (or until aborted with
fnref	sm_play_tone_abort),
	the parameter
ref	duration
	should be set to zero. Otherwise
ref	duration
	should be set to the required tone duration in milliseconds.
	<p>
	The
ref	wait_for_completion
	flag may be set by the application in which case this API call
	will not return until the tone has been completely output,
	however no other Prosody API function can be performed on the
	channel during this waiting period.
	Obviously setting this flag is not useful when the tone has been
	specified as being a continuous tone
	since there would then be no way to stop the tone.
	See the document <a href="../an-wait_for_completion.html">Prosody
	application note: waiting for completion</a> for examples of
	how to wait without blocking other functions.
	<p>
	Alternatively the application can wait to be notified by an
	event that tone generation of a given duration has completed.
	When a write event has been associated with channel (see
	<a href="apifn-sm_channel_set_event.html">sm_channel_set_event</a>),
	then the driver will notify the application with that event
	whenever it needs to invoke
fnref	sm_play_tone_status.
	<p>
	This requires the module
modref	tonegen
	to have been downloaded.
	<p>
	The channel is reserved for playing the tone until the API has
	reported completion. If the
ref	wait_for_completion
	flag is set, then the API considers that completion has been
	reported when this API function returns, otherwise completion
	is reported only by
fnref	sm_play_tone_status
	returning the status
	<a href="apifn-sm_play_tone_status.html#field-kSMPlayToneStatusComplete">
	kSMPlayToneStatusComplete</a>. In this case the
	application <strong>must</strong> call
fnref	sm_play_tone_status
	repeatedly until it reports completion. It should use an event
	on the channel to notify it when to check the status.
	No other output activity can take place on the channel until the
	completion of the tone has been reported, Note that the event
	itself does not indicate completion of the tone. It is possible
	for the event to be signalled even if the tone has not yet
	completed, so it is essential that the application checks the
	status and continues waiting if the tone has not completed.
explain
	0
retval
error	ERR_SM_DEVERR - device error
error	ERR_SM_BAD_PARAMETER - unknown tone or inconsistent parameters

