apifn	sm_add_input_tone_set
params	sm_input_tone_set_parms tonesetp
	The module to which the tone set is to be added.
field	tSMModuleId module in
	One more than the identifier of the first tone in band 1.
field	tSM_INT band1_first_freq_coeffs_id in
	The number of tones in band 1.
field	tSM_INT band1_freq_count in
	One more than the identifier of the first tone in band 2.
field	tSM_INT band2_first_freq_coeffs_id in
	The number of tones in band 2.
field	tSM_INT band2_freq_count in
	The maximum power of the third loudest frequency. If the third
	frequency exceeds this, then it prevents detection of a
	tone. This is specified as a factor so, for example, the
	value <code>0.1</code> indicates that the third frequency must
	be no stronger than a tenth the power of the second frequency.
field	double req_third_peak in
	The minimum signal to noise ratio. This is given as a factor
	to be multiplied by the total power. For example, the value
	<code>0.25</code> means that the detected signal must be more
	than a quarter of the total received power.
field	double req_signal_to_noise_ratio in
	The minimum power. For dual tones this is the power of the
	tone with the lesser amplitude.
field	double req_minimum_power in
	The maximum twist. This is the ratio of power between the two
	components of a dual tone. For example, a value of
	<code>10</code> means that the stronger must be no more than
	ten times the power of the weaker.
field	double req_twist_for_dual_tone in
	The identifier of this tone set.
field	tSM_INT id out
unstruct
	This call may be used to define an additional set of simple
	input tones (recognisable on any input channel) for the
	specified module
ref	module.
	<p>
	The new set of input tones is defined with respect to two sets
	of possible component frequencies, band 1 and band 2, and
	various other parameters
ref	req_third_peak,
ref	req_signal_to_noise_ratio,
ref	req_minimum_power
	and
ref	req_twist_for_dual_tone.
	<p>
	Band 1 is comprised of
ref	band1_freq_count
	coefficients whose ids range from:
ref	band1_first_freq_coeffs_id
	to
ref	band1_first_freq_coeffs_id
	+
ref	band1_freq_count
	- 1
	<p>
	Similarly Band 2 is comprised of
ref	band2_freq_count
	coefficients whose ids range from:
ref	band2_first_freq_coeffs_id
	to
ref	band2_first_freq_coeffs_id
	+
ref	band2_freq_count
	- 1
	<p>
	The new set of input tones will consist of all those tones that
	have a component frequency that is within the limits for a
	frequency coefficient pair taken from band 1, and another that
	is within the limits for a frequency coefficient pair taken from
	band 2.
	<p>
	For example, if band 1 was defined as the set of input frequency
	coefficient ids {0,1,2,3} and band 2 was defined as {4,5,6,7},
	then the defined input tone set would be:
	<p><table>
	<tr> <td>{</td>
		<td>&lt;0,4&gt;,</td> <td>&lt;0,5&gt;,</td>
		<td>&lt;0,6&gt;,</td> <td>&lt;0,7&gt;,</td>
	</tr>
	<tr> <td></td>
		<td>&lt;1,4&gt;,</td> <td>&lt;1,5&gt;,</td>
		<td>&lt;1,6&gt;,</td> <td>&lt;1,7&gt;,</td>
	</tr>
	<tr> <td></td>
		<td>&lt;2,4&gt;,</td> <td>&lt;2,5&gt;,</td>
		<td>&lt;2,6&gt;,</td> <td>&lt;2,7&gt;,</td>
	</tr>
	<tr> <td></td>
		<td>&lt;3,4&gt;,</td> <td>&lt;3,5&gt;,</td>
		<td>&lt;3,6&gt;,</td> <td>&lt;3,7&gt;</td>
	<td>}</td>
	</tr>
	</table>
	<p>
	On return
ref	id
	will be set to an identifier for the new set of input tones.
	This id may be used as a parameter to
fnref	sm_listen_for
	in order to specify the new set of input tones as those to be
	recognised on an input channel.
	<p>
	If single tones (as opposed to dual tones) are required to be
	detected, then either
ref	band1_freq_count
	or
ref	band2_freq_count
	should be set to zero. In this case the corresponding
ref	band1_first_freq_coeffs_id
	or
ref	band2_first_freq_coeffs_id
	is ignored.
	<p>
	See
	<a href="../prospapi_intones.html">
	Prosody speech processing: pre-loaded input tones</a>
	for list of predefined input frequency
	coefficient pairs, and for list of predefined input tone
	sets.
	See
	<a href="../tonedet.html">Prosody - Details of Tone Detection Algorithm</a>
	for an explanation of the other parameters to this call.
	<p>
explain
	0
