	The upper frequency boundary (in Hz).
field	double upper_limit in
	The lower frequency boundary (in Hz).
field	double lower_limit in
unstruct
	A beep will be recognised if it lasts for at least
ref	min_duration
	milliseconds and the frequency is between
ref lower_limit
	and
ref	upper_limit.
	<p>
	When a beep is recognised, the recognition event associated with the
	channel is set and the application can then retrieve the details
	for the recognised beep by calling
fnref	sm_get_recognised.
	<p>
	Setting
ref	min_duration
	to zero disables the detection.
	<p>
	The modules
modref	td
	and
modref	beepdet
	are required.
explain
	0
retval

